# Hermetic Supabase credentials for local E2E only — NOT a real project.
# Read by scripts/build-e2e.mjs (`npm run build:e2e`) and playwright.config.ts.
#
# Why these values are safe:
#   - isSupabaseConfigured() only requires an https <project>.supabase.co
#     host, so this host passes the guard and account-gated UI renders.
#   - Signed-out flows (what the E2E suite exercises) never touch the
#     network: supabase-js resolves the session from localStorage and returns
#     null. Only real sign-in/submissions would contact the host.
#   - CI ignores this file entirely and builds with the real GitHub secrets.
#
# Local flow for Supabase-gated E2E (favorites gate, login dialog, account UI):
#   cp .env.e2e.example .env.e2e     # optional — the example already works
#   npm run build:e2e                # bake Supabase config like CI does
#   npm run test:e2e:core            # or: npx playwright test <spec>
#
# Have a real Supabase project? Copy this file to .env.e2e (gitignored) and
# replace both values with the ones from your project dashboard.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://ventu-local-e2e.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=local-e2e-anon-key-never-contacted
